Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250: Fix PCIe wake GPIO polarity

PCIe WAKE# is an active-low signal per the PCIe base spec, but sm8250.dtsi
declares all three controllers' wake-gpios as GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH.

BACKPORT of patch 6/34 from Krishna Chaitanya Chundru's "arm64: dts: qcom:
Move PCIe phy/GPIOs to root port nodes and fix wake-gpios polarity",
2026-09-10, UNMERGED at the time of writing:
https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260910-root_port-v1-0-90a252ddbbfa@oss.qualcomm.com

WHY THIS ONE NEEDS A PATCH WHEN SM8550/SM8650 DID NOT. Those two SoCs keep
wake-gpios in the BOARD files, so upstream's equivalent patches touch
sm8550-hdk/mtp/qrd and sm8650-hdk/mtp/qrd etc. -- files we do not build. Our
own board DTS carries them instead, and they were corrected directly. sm8250
is the exception: its wake-gpios live in the SoC dtsi we take from the
tarball, so inheriting the fix requires carrying it.

Affects Pocket Max, AYN Thor Lite and the Retroid boards, all of which put
their wifi@0 under &pcieport0 on pcie0. pcie1/pcie2 are changed too, to
match upstream exactly rather than to fix anything we use.

CAVEAT, same as the board-side change: the series is unmerged and its cover
says "No Fixes tag is added as no functional issue has been observed", so
the expected result is no visible change. WAKE is a suspend/resume signal --
a wrong polarity hides until the device is suspended, so this wants a
suspend/resume cycle on an SM8250 board, not just a boot.

DROP THIS PATCH once the series lands in the pinned stable series -- grep
sm8250.dtsi for `wake-gpios.*GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH`, which must return nothing.

---

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
@@ -2202,7 +2202,7 @@
 			phy-names = "pciephy";
 
 			perst-gpios = <&tlmm 79 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
-			wake-gpios = <&tlmm 81 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+			wake-gpios = <&tlmm 81 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 			pinctrl-names = "default";
 			pinctrl-0 = <&pcie0_default_state>;
@@ -2329,7 +2329,7 @@
 			phy-names = "pciephy";
 
 			perst-gpios = <&tlmm 82 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
-			wake-gpios = <&tlmm 84 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+			wake-gpios = <&tlmm 84 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 			pinctrl-names = "default";
 			pinctrl-0 = <&pcie1_default_state>;
@@ -2456,7 +2456,7 @@
 			phy-names = "pciephy";
 
 			perst-gpios = <&tlmm 85 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
-			wake-gpios = <&tlmm 87 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+			wake-gpios = <&tlmm 87 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 			pinctrl-names = "default";
 			pinctrl-0 = <&pcie2_default_state>;
